  "question": {
    "text": "<p>The material filled between the plates of a parallel plate capacitor has resistivity <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>200</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>&#937;</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></math>. The value of capacitance of the capacitor is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>pF</mi></math>. If a potential difference of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>40</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi></math> is applied across the plates of the capacitor, then the value of leakage current flowing out of the capacitor is: (given the value of relative permittivity of material is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>50</mn></math>)</p>"
  },
